-- title:
--   Bounded exponent for torsion in a tree lattice in PGL₂
-- statement:
--   Let $R_0$ be a discrete valuation ring (a commutative domain with the `IsDiscreteValuationRing` structure) whose residue field is finite, and let $K_0$ be a field equipped with an $R_0$-algebra structure making it the fraction field of $R_0$. Let $\Delta$ be a subgroup of $\mathrm{PGL}(2, K_0)$, acting through the Bruhat–Tits tree `BruhatTits.tree R₀ K₀`: the simple graph whose vertices are the homothety classes of full $R_0$-lattices in $K_0^2$ (the quotient of `FullLattice R₀ K₀` by the homothety setoid) and whose adjacency is generated by the relation that $x$ and $y$ admit representing full lattices $L$, $L'$ with `AdjacentLattice L L'`. Assume that for every dart $d$ of this tree (every edge with a chosen orientation) the stabiliser of $d$ in $\Delta$ is finite, and that the set of $\Delta$-orbits on vertices, `Mumford.QuotVert ↥Δ (LT.LatticeTree.Vertex R₀ K₀)`, is finite. Then there exists a natural number $m$ with $0 < m$ such that $\gamma^m = 1$ for every $\gamma \in \Delta$ of finite order; that is, the torsion of $\Delta$ has bounded exponent.
--
--   This is the statement that a lattice in $\mathrm{PGL}_2$ over a local field, acting on the Bruhat–Tits tree with finite dart stabilisers and finitely many vertex orbits, has torsion of bounded exponent, as in Serre's theory of groups acting on trees. It is the companion of the corresponding bound for elements fixing a vertex, and is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development, where a uniform exponent for the torsion of $\Delta$ is needed to produce functions on the rigid-analytic quotient with prescribed vanishing.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_BruhatTits_exists_pos_forall_isOfFinOrder_pow_eq_one.lean

